# What gets pushed: source code, configs, docs, scripts, small result files, and the
# two runtime files main.py loads (voice_emotion_model.h5, label_encoder.pkl).
# What never gets pushed: personal data, secrets, environments, datasets, trained
# models, downloaded audio. `git add .` is safe - anything below is skipped.

# ---- Personal data and secrets (NEVER commit) ----
backend/data/
.env*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.key
*.pem

# ---- Environments and dependencies ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
node_modules/

# ---- Datasets (re-download with ./train_all.sh or the fetch scripts) ----
**/datasets/*
!**/datasets/README.md
# A set we switched off still sits on disk under datasets_disabled/. It is a
# download, not source, and esconv/EmpatheticDialogues are CC-BY-NC, so it must
# never land in a public repo.
**/datasets_disabled/
backend/eval/data/
backend/chat_training/data/
backend/distress_training/data/

# ---- Trained models and weights (share via Hugging Face, not git) ----
backend/distress_training/model*/
backend/chat_training/adapters*/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.npz
*.h5
*.pkl
!backend/voice_emotion_model.h5
!backend/label_encoder.pkl

# ---- Audio (voice notes, eval clips, recordings) ----
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.webm

# ---- Build output, caches, logs ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log

# ---- Editor / OS / local tooling ----
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/settings.local.json
